cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuroTCS in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "NeuroTCS / temporalmetric: Citation-locked, fail-closed longitudinal medical AI audit framework"
abstract: >-
  NeuroTCS is a citation-locked, fail-closed framework for auditing the
  temporal coherence of longitudinal medical AI predictions against
  internationally endorsed published clinical guidelines for Alzheimer's
  disease (AD). As of v1.9.0 the framework is scope-narrowed to AD-only
  in preparation for FDA Q-Submission (target Q1 2027); non-AD disease
  packs (PD, MS, oncology, stroke, lung nodule) that previously shipped
  in v1.7.x have been extracted to seed future per-disease repositories
  post-FDA-clearance. The framework comprises seven core engineering
  pieces plus five v1.7.0 methodological modules: (1) categorical input
  contract, (2) continuous-biomarker input contract with UCUM unit
  enforcement, (3) citation-locked AD rule packs (NIA-AA 2018 Framework,
  AA 2024 Revised Criteria with Jack 2024 Table 7 integrated biological
  + clinical staging, AA 2024 TRAC framework for anti-Aβ therapy
  trajectories), (4) audit core library (cTCS / pTCS / uTCS with cluster
  bootstrap, BCa intervals, and Huber M-estimation), (5) FHIR Observation
  output schema (roadmap v1.9.x+), (6) reference dataset adapters (ADNI,
  OASIS-3, NACC, MIRIAD shipped with byte-exact four-cohort triangulation
  lock), and (7) synthetic-trajectory validation harness (roadmap
  v1.9.x+). v1.7.0 added Riley 2024 sample-size, FUTURE-AI fairness +
  robustness panels, Kwong 2022 silent-deployment, multi-dimensional
  scanner factorial, and empirical operational threshold derivation.
  Schema v1.3.0 distinguishes guideline_quote from clinical_inference
  attribution. v1.8.0 hallmark result: four-cohort triangulation
  byte-exact across OASIS-3 (0.994191), ADNI (0.994575), NACC (0.991502),
  MIRIAD (0.985369), with max pairwise ΔcTCS = 0.009206 (all 6 pairs ≤
  0.01 world-class threshold).
